{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}How It Works — ISDS Thematic Watcher{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<section class="page-head">
  <h1>How the instrument works</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The chart below is the whole instrument on one page, drawn directly from the
    repository it describes. Reading top to bottom: the nine public sources we check
    every run; the automated pipeline that collects, de-duplicates, scores, and
    quality-gates each candidate development; the council of AI research agents
    (each box names its model) that interprets the week under binding
    fact-verification gates; the researcher's own verification column — no claim is
    stated as fact without a human check against its original source; and the
    deliverables each Monday. The moving dots show work flowing through the system.
    Hover any box for its full description and the exact code behind it.
  </p>
</section>
<figure class="workflow-figure">
  <div class="workflow-scroll">
    {{ workflow_svg | safe }}
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Generated deterministically from the same manifest that renders this chart in
    the project's research vault; every box and arrow cites the file that
    implements it.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
{% endblock %}
